
<p>The third developer betas of Apple’s 27 OSes dropped today, and this new page in Apple’s developer documentation drew my attention — a built-in Uniform Type Identifier for Markdown data:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p><strong>UTI:</strong> <code>net.daringfireball.markdown</code></p>

<p><strong>Conforms to:</strong> <code>public.utf8-plain-text</code></p>
</blockquote>

<p>I had previously recommended conforming to <code>public.plain-text</code> but stated that the text encoding should be UTF-8. I’ve updated <a href="https://daringfireball.net/linked/2011/08/05/markdown-uti">my own recommendation</a> to <code>public.utf8-plain-text</code> to enshrine the UTF-8 encoding. (Back in 2004 UTF-8 support was far from universal. Today it is.)</p>

